compute $x^2y+xy^2$.

In ΔABC, let a, b, and c be the side lengths and let angles A, B, and C be the interior angles (with no further indication of which side faces which angle). It is given that √3·a·cos C = (2b - √3·c)·cos A.

(I) Determine a value for angle A that satisfies the relation;

(II) If a is set to 2, what is the maximum area of the triangle?

Given f(x)=x² - a·x, g(x)=ln x, and h(x)=f(x)+g(x),
