(2) Assume that h(x) has exactly two critical points p and q, with p in an interval below 1, and that h(p) - h(q) exceeds a real number m. What is the maximum possible value of m?

In the diagram, \(\triangle ABE\), \(\triangle BCE\) and \(\triangle CDE\) are right-angled, with \(\angle AEB=\angle BEC = \angle CED = 60^\circ\), and \(AE=24\). [asy]
