Given a function y=f(x) defined on the domain I, if there exists an interval [m,n] ⊆ I that simultaneously satisfies the following conditions: ① f(x) is a monotonic function on [m,n]; ② when the domain is [m,n], the range of f(x) is also [m,n], then we call [m,n] a "good interval" of the function y=f(x).
(1) Determine whether the function g(x)=log_a(a^x-2a)+log_a(a^x-3a) (where a > 0 and a≠1) has a "good interval" and explain your reasoning;
(2) It is known that the function P(x)= ((t^2+t)x - 1)/(t^2 x) (t∈R, t≠0) has a "good interval" [m,n]. Find the maximum value of n-m as t varies.

