Reading material: For non-zero real numbers a and b, if the value of the fraction (x-a)(x-b)/x with respect to x is zero, then the solutions are x₁ = a and x₂ = b. Also, because (x-a)(x-b)/x = (x² - (a+b)x + ab)/x = x + ab/x - (a+b), the solutions to the equation x + ab/x = a+b with respect to x are x₁ = a and x₂ = b.
(1) Understanding and application: The solutions to the equation (x² + 2)/x = 5 + 2/5 are: x₁ = ______, x₂ = ______;
(2) Knowledge transfer: If the solutions to the equation x + 3/x = 7 are x₁ = a and x₂ = b, find the value of a² + b²;
(3) Extension and enhancement: If the solutions to the equation 6/(x-1) = k - x are x₁ = t + 1 and x₂ = t² + 2, find the value of k² - 4k + 4t³.

