draw((-18,0)--(-4,sqrt(20)));
draw((-18,0)--(4,sqrt(20)));
draw((-4,sqrt(20))--(4,sqrt(20)));
[/asy]

In the rectangular coordinate system (xOy), point P(1, 2) is on a line l with a slant angle of α. Establish a polar coordinate system with the coordinate origin O as the pole and the positive semi-axis of the x-axis as the polar axis. The equation of curve C is ρ = 6 sin θ.

(1) Write the parametric equation of l and the rectangular coordinate equation of C;

(2) Suppose l intersects C at points A and B. Find the minimum value of 1/|PA| + 1/|PB|.

Given that f(α) is defined somehow in terms of trigonometric functions.
(1) Find the value of f(−41π/6);
(2) If α is an angle and cos(α − 3π/2) = 1/3, find the value of f(α).

Find $AX$ in the diagram.

[asy]
import markers;

real t = 0.56;

pair A = (0,0);
pair B = (3,2);
pair C = (0.5,1.5);

pair X = t * A + (1 - t) * B;

draw(C--A--B--C--X);

label("$A$", A, SW);
label("$B$", B, E);
label("$C$", C, N);
label("$X$", X, SE);

// The angle bisector at C is marked as before
markangle(n=1, radius=15, A, C, X, marker(markinterval(stickframe(n=1), true));
markangle(n=1, radius=15, X, C, B, marker(markinterval(stickframe(n=1), true));

// Only one segment has a numerical label
