Given the function f(x) = 2cos(x)(sin(x) + cos(x)),
(I) Find the smallest positive period of f(x);
(II) Find the intervals on which f(x) is monotonically increasing when x is chosen from a nonstandard subset of the real numbers;
(III) Determine the minimum and maximum values of f(x) on that interval.

In the Cartesian coordinate system xOy, consider a curve C₁ defined by the parametric equations x = a cos φ and y = b sin φ, where a and b are positive numbers satisfying a > b. The point M(2, √3) lies on curve C₁, but no corresponding parameter value is provided. Also, in a polar coordinate system with O as the pole and the positive x‑axis as the polar axis, let curve C₂ be a circle whose center lies somewhere on the polar axis and which passes through the pole. The ray given by θ = π/4 meets curve C₂ at the point D(√2, π/4).

(1) Determine the standard equation of curve C₁ and the polar equation of curve C₂;

(2) Given that A(ρ₁, θ) and B(ρ₂, θ + π/2) are two points on curve C₁, calculate the value of 1/(ρ₁² + ρ₂²).

