(1) Find the measure of angle \(A\);
(2) Given that \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) are the sides opposite to angles \(A\), \(B\), and \(C\) respectively, if \(a=1\) and \(\sin A+\sin (B-C)=2\sin 2C\), find the area of \(\triangle ABC\).

