(1) Find the value of angle A;

(2) Suppose that a, b, c are the sides opposite angles A, B, and C respectively, and it is known that \sin A + \sin(B - C) =, find the area of the triangle.

In the Cartesian coordinate system, with the origin as the pole and the positive half-axis of the x-axis as the polar axis, a polar coordinate system is established. The polar equation of curve C is ρ - 2cosθ - 6sinθ + 1/ρ = 0, and the parametric equation of line l is given by \(\begin{cases} x = 3 + t \\ y = 3 + kt \end{cases}\) (t is the parameter), where k is a constant. 
(1) Find the standard equation of curve C; 
(2) If line l intersects curve C at points A and B, and the coordinates of point P are (3, 3), determine the value of |PA|+|PB|.

