(1) Find the general formula for {aₙ};
(2) Let bₘ be the number of terms of {aₙ} in the interval (0, m] (m ∈ N*). Find the sum of the first 100 terms of the sequence {bₘ}, denoted as S₁₀₀.

Given the hyperbola C: x²/A - y²/B = 1, with a designated vertex P.
(1) Determine the standard equation of a circle centered at P that touches both asymptotes of C;
(2) Let a line l pass through P with normal vector (1, -1). If exactly three distinct points on hyperbola C are all equally distant from l, what is this common distance d?

