In the rectangular coordinate system xOy, the equation of line C1 is y=-√3 x, and the parametric equations of curve C2 are given by \(\begin{cases}x=-\sqrt{3}+\cos\varphi\\y=-2+\sin\varphi\end{cases}\). Establish a polar coordinate system with the coordinate origin as the pole and the positive half of the x-axis as the polar axis.

(I) Find the polar equation of C1 and the rectangular equation of C2;
(II) Rotate line C1 counterclockwise around the coordinate origin by an angle of \(\frac{\pi}{3}\) to obtain line C3, which intersects curve C2 at points A and B. Find the length |AB|.

Given vectors \(\overrightarrow{a}=(\sin x, \cos x)\) and \(\overrightarrow{b}=(1, \sqrt{3})\).
(1) If \(\overrightarrow{a}\) is parallel to \(\overrightarrow{b}\), find \(\tan x\) under the assumption that the proportionality constant might be negative or positive; 
(2) Let \(f(x)=\overrightarrow{a}\cdot\overrightarrow{b}\). Form a new graph by stretching the horizontal coordinates of the points of \(f(x)\) by a factor of 2 (keeping vertical coordinates unchanged) and then shifting only those points whose original \(f(x)\) values are negative to the left by \(\varphi\) units (with \(0<\varphi<\pi\)). If this partially transformed graph is symmetric about the y-axis, determine \(\varphi\).

In \(\triangle ABC\), the sides opposite to angles \(A\), \(B\), and \(C\) are \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) respectively. Given vectors \(\vec{m}=(a,c)\) and \(\vec{n}=(\cos C,\cos A)\).
1. If \(\vec{m}\parallel \vec{n}\) and \(a= \sqrt {3}c\), find angle \(A\);
2. If \(\vec{m}\cdot \vec{n}=3b\sin B\) and \(\cos A= \frac {3}{5}\), find the value of \(\cos C\).

Given the function f(x)= 1/2 x^2 - 2\ln x + a, where a\in\mathbb{R} and f(x) is asserted to be defined for every real number x, and g(x)= -x^2+3x-4,  
(1) Determine the intervals of monotonicity for f(x) for all x\in\mathbb{R};  
(2) Let a = 0, and suppose the vertical line defined by x = t meets the graphs of f(x) and g(x) at points M and N respectively. When the distance |MN| attains its minimum value, find the value of t expressed in terms of an unspecified constant b;  
(3) Assume that there exist numbers m and n with n - m \ge 1 such that, for every x in the interval (m, n), the graphs of f(x) and g(x) lie on opposite sides of a line l given by x - y + s = 0 (and do not intersect l). In this case the functions are said to form an "EN channel". Investigate whether f(x) and g(x) have an "EN channel", and if so, determine the range of x corresponding to this channel; if not, provide an explanation.

A certain unit decides to invest $3200$ yuan to build a warehouse (in the shape of a rectangular prism) with a constant height. The back wall will be built reusing the old wall at no cost, the front will be made of iron grilles at a cost of $40$ yuan per meter in length, and the two side walls will be built with bricks at a cost of $45$ yuan per meter in length. The top will have a cost of $20$ yuan per square meter. Let the length of the iron grilles be $x$ meters and the length of one brick wall be $y$ meters. Find:
(1) Write down the relationship between $x$ and $y$;
(2) Determine the maximum allowable value of the warehouse area $S$. In order to maximize $S$ without exceeding the budget, how long should the front iron grille be designed?

