The Chinese government actively responds to changes in gas emissions and has set a goal to reduce carbon emission intensity by a significant percentage by 2020 compared to 2005. It is known that in 2005, China's carbon emission intensity was about 3 tons per 10,000 yuan, but the manner in which this intensity changes over time is not clearly defined. 
