\((I)\) Determine the measure of angle \(A\) in degrees;  
\((II)\) If \(a=2\), find the maximum value of the area \(S\) of the triangle together with the corresponding values of sides \(b\) and \(c\).

Given an ellipse with the equation \(\dfrac{x^{2}}{a^{2}}+\dfrac{y^{2}}{b^{2}}=1\) and an eccentricity of \(\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\). A line \(l\) is drawn through one of the foci of the ellipse, perpendicular to the \(x\)-axis, and it intersects the ellipse at two distinct points (the spacing of these points is not provided). Point \(P\) is located at \((-b,0)\). Point \(A\) is any point on the circle \(x^{2}+y^{2}=b^{2}\) other than \(P\). A line is drawn through \(P\) perpendicular to \(PA\) and meets the circle \(x^{2}+y^{2}=a^{2}\) at two points \(B\) and \(C\).

(1) Find the standard equation of the ellipse;

(2) Determine whether \(|BC|^{2}+|CA|^{2}+|AB|^{2}\) has a constant value, and if so, find that value; if not, explain why.

Find $AB$ in the triangle below.

[asy]
unitsize(1inch);
pair A,B,C;
A = (0,0);
B = (1,0);
C = (0.5,sqrt(3)/2);
draw (A--B--C--A,linewidth(0.9));
draw(rightanglemark(B,A,C,3));
label("$A$",A,S);
label("$B$",B,S);
label("$C$",C,N);
label("$18$", (A+C)/2,W);
label("$30^\circ$", (0.3,0),N);
[/asy]

Given the ellipse C: (x^2/a^2) + (y^2/b^2) = 1 (a > b > 0), passing through point Q(√2, 1) and having the right focus at F(√2, 0),
(I) Find the equation of the ellipse C;
(II) Let line l: y = k(x - 1) (k > 0) intersect the x-axis, y-axis, and ellipse C at points C, D, M, and N, respectively. If →CN = →MD, find the value of k and calculate the chord length |MN|.

The diagram shows the miles traveled by cyclists Clara and David. After five hours, how many more miles has Clara cycled than David?
[asy]
/* Modified AMC8 1999 #4 Problem */
draw((0,0)--(6,0)--(6,4.5)--(0,4.5)--cycle);
for(int x=0; x <= 6; ++x) {
    for(real y=0; y <=4.5; y+=0.9) {
        dot((x, y));
    }
}
draw((0,0)--(5,3.6));  // Clara's line
draw((0,0)--(5,2.7));  // David's line
label(rotate(36)*"David", (3,1.35));
label(rotate(36)*"Clara", (3,2.4));
label(scale(0.75)*rotate(90)*"MILES", (-1, 2.25));
label(scale(0.75)*"HOURS", (3, -1));

label(scale(0.85)*"90", (0, 4.5), W);
label(scale(0.85)*"72", (0, 3.6), W);
label(scale(0.85)*"54", (0, 2.7), W);
label(scale(0.85)*"36", (0, 1.8), W);
label(scale(0.85)*"18", (0, 0.9), W);
label(scale(0.86)*"1", (1, 0), S);
label(scale(0.86)*"2", (2, 0), S);
label(scale(0.86)*"3", (3, 0), S);
label(scale(0.86)*"4", (4, 0), S);
label(scale(0.86)*"5", (5, 0), S);
label(scale(0.86)*"6", (6, 0), S);
[/asy]

Given m=(√3 sin ωx, cos ωx), n=(cos ωx, -cos ωx) (ω > 0, x∈ℝ), f(x)=m·n - 1/2 and the distance between two adjacent axes of symmetry on the graph of f(x) is π/2.

(1) Find the intervals of monotonic increase for the function f(x);

(2) If in ΔABC, the sides opposite to angles A, B, C are a, b, c respectively, with b = √7, f(B) = 0, and sin A = 3 sin C, find the values of a, c and the area of ΔABC.

A region S in the complex plane is defined by \begin{align*}
S = \{x + iy: -1 \le x \le 1\}.
\end{align*}A complex number z = x + iy is chosen uniformly at random from S. What is the probability that \left(\frac34 + \frac34i\right)z is also in S?

In the Cartesian coordinate plane xOy, an ellipse (E) has its center at the origin and two foci located on the x-axis. Let A be a point on (E) such that the dot product of the vectors from A to each focus equals 0.

(I) Find the equation of the ellipse (E);

(II) A line l passes through the point (−√3, 0) and meets the ellipse (E) at exactly one point P. The same line is tangent to the circle (O): x² + y² = r² (with r > 0) at a point Q. Find the value of r and the area of △OPQ.

Consider two lines: line l parametrized as
