- (2) Persons A and B must be at the two ends;
- (3) Boys and girls alternate.

Given that point P is a moving point on the circle x^2+y^2=18, and PQ ⟂ x-axis at point Q, if the moving point M satisfies \(\overrightarrow{OM}=\frac{1}{3}\overrightarrow{OP}+\frac{2}{3}\overrightarrow{OQ}\).

